Criteria 1, 2, 3 and 4 for koniz-dev/flutter-starter#127
=====================================================

$ flutter test test/core/network/forced_logout_session_test.dart --reporter expanded

Run on the merged fix (cf18772). This is the per-test detail that
tests.log cannot show: run_acceptance.sh trims the full-suite log to a
head+tail excerpt, and these five tests sit in the elided middle.

Each test assembles the real provider graph - real ApiClient, real
interceptor chain, real AuthNotifier restored by the production
restoreSession() - and swaps only the two platform-channel storage
services and the HTTP transport. The refresh fails through production
code (no refresh token stored), not a stub.

  criterion 1 -> "a 401 whose refresh fails clears AuthState.user"
                 "the retry-exhausted logout branch clears AuthState.user too"
  criterion 2 -> "a forced logout moves the running app to /login"
                 (router mounted; see also forced_logout_before/after.png)
  criterion 3 -> "building the API client does not build the auth notifier"
  criterion 4 -> "a 401 after the container is disposed does not throw"

The app's own logging boxes have been stripped for readability; the
"API Request: GET /users/me" line each test emits is the 401 being driven.

00:00 +0: forced logout drops the in-memory session (#127 criterion 1) a 401 whose refresh fails clears AuthState.user
00:00 +1: forced logout drops the in-memory session (#127 criterion 1) the retry-exhausted logout branch clears AuthState.user too
00:00 +2: no DI cycle is introduced (#127 criterion 3) building the API client does not build the auth notifier
00:00 +3: the router reacts without a restart (#127 criterion 2) a forced logout moves the running app to /login
00:03 +4: a forced logout with nobody listening is harmless (#127 c4) a 401 after the container is disposed does not throw
00:03 +5: All tests passed!
